    "body": "I looked into this a bit and as far as I can tell this isn't related to the dispatch algorithm. It's about the activation behavior of the label element only.\r\n\r\nWhen the label element is associated with a checkbox, either via nesting or the for attribute, and its activation behavior is triggered, user agents dispatch a (new) click event on the checkbox. (There are some differences here, e.g., `new MouseEvent(\"click\", {button:2}` [does not trigger activation behavior](https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/6845) of the label element in Firefox, but does in other browsers.)\r\n\r\nTo completely remove platform-dependent behavior however we'd have to test how this works for all form controls a `label` element can be associated with, as the activation behavior might well differ.",
